cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the preprint below."
title: "Helly-Type Combinatorial Configurations of Lattice Triangles: Exact Structure and Asymptotics"
abstract: >-
  Source, computational verification scripts and exact data for the paper.
  An Euler-characteristic transfer theorem encodes the counting function
  f(n,k) of intersecting families of lattice triangles in a single signed
  depth spectrum of the grid line arrangement; the continuum constant p_2 is
  evaluated exactly as 191/300; and the closed/open discrepancy is shown to be
  of exact order n^10 log n for k = 2.
